      "description": "DSD Renewables, legally Distributed Solar Development, LLC, is a Schenectady-based U.S. distributed-energy platform that develops, finances, acquires, owns and operates commercial, industrial, municipal and community solar, storage and EV-charging infrastructure. The business began as GE Solar in 2012 and became the standalone DSD platform in 2019 with backing from BlackRock's Global Renewable Power II strategy. BlackRock acquired GE Renewable Energy's remaining interest in November 2020. Ares Management invested $200 million through its Infrastructure and Power strategy in March 2022 and became majority owner after a 2025 change-of-control and common-equity conversion. Cox Enterprises made a $250 million minority strategic investment in November 2023. July 2025 DSD materials identify Ares, BlackRock and Cox as current platform backers; exact current percentages are not publicly disclosed. DSD reported $238 million of financing for 188 operating distributed-generation projects totaling 233 MW in August 2025. Individual projects, project SPVs, financing counterparties and the BlackRock/GIP manager combination are outside the canonical PortCo boundary. No signed or completed DSD platform sale was identified through August 15, 2026.",
